; Wendy 2 (wendy2c), the W65C02S board with banked RAM: the emulator's `--machine wendy2c`
; (emulator/README.md), run with `--wendy2-prog FILE --load 4000`, which preloads the program
; into RAM and starts it there, skipping the serial boot. lathe/docs/boards.md has the recipe.
;
; In the bank configuration it starts in ($01 on VIA port B, bits 0-4) $0000-$EFFF is flat
; RAM, the VIA is at $F000 (the 16x2 LCD is on its ports) and $F800-$FFFF is RAM again, the
; vectors included: a program that wants interrupts writes its handler's address to $FFFE.
; The preloaded program must stay below $F000. There are no host services: a program shows
; its output on the LCD and ends with STP, which ends the run.
cpu       65c02
zeropage  $00 $FF
code      $4000 $EFFF
data      $0200 $3FFF
stack     $FF
exit      stop
output    raw         ; the file is the code from $4000, and the load address is $start
